# Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

Source: [playwright-accessibility-testing](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) — UI principles, not test boilerplate

## Semantic HTML
- One `<h1>` per page; heading hierarchy must not skip levels
- Use `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<aside>`, `<section>` with accessible names via `aria-label` when needed
- Buttons for actions; links for navigation — never `<div onClick>`

## Keyboard & focus
- All interactive controls reachable via Tab; visible focus ring (`focus-visible:ring-2`)
- Modals/drawers trap focus and restore on close
- Skip link to main content on dashboard shell

## ARIA & live regions
- `aria-live="polite"` for WebSocket telemetry streams and alert counts
- Icon-only buttons require `aria-label`
- Charts: provide text summary or table fallback for screen readers

## Color & contrast
- Text ≥ 4.5:1 contrast on dark surfaces; large text ≥ 3:1
- Never convey severity by color alone — pair with icon + text label (existing `SeverityBadge` pattern)
- Test heatmap cells with `title` or `aria-label` describing date and intensity

## Responsive & motion
- Layouts usable at 320px width; touch targets ≥ 44×44px
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; disable non-essential Framer Motion when set

## Forms
- Every input has `<Label htmlFor>`; errors linked via `aria-describedby`
- Loading states announced with `aria-busy` where appropriate
